:"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T11:35:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T12:19:22Z","body":"You haven't set up your signals correctly. The signal is only hooked up for the body that you've manually placed in `test_sleeping.tscn`, but you need to hook up the signal inside of `test_sleeping_state_change_cube.tscn` instead, so that every instantiated body has it.\n\n~~On top of that you're manually changing the `sleeping` property through the inspector in your video, which as mentioned in [the documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_rigidbody3d.html#class-rigidbody3d-signal-sleeping-state-changed) won't cause the `sleeping_state_changed` signal to be emitted, as it's only emitted when the physics engine decides to put the body to sleep.~~\n\nEDIT: Sorry, I missed the last part of your description.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2639577669/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645838661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102107#issuecomment-2645838661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102107","id":2645838661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dtEtF","user":{"login":"ayt4797","id":54717651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NzE3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54717651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797","html_url":"https://github.com/ayt4797","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayt4797/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T16:48:48Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T16:48:48Z","body":"Ok, does that have to be in code? or with the signal editor? I was able to fix it by doing it in code such that every instantated object is connected to the rigidbodies signal, but if your suggesting I just applied the signal to the wrong scene in the signal editor that would be better. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645838661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645843914","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102107#issuecomment-2645843914","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102107","id":2645843914,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dtF_K","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OD